      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-252481",
      ":question/problem": "Three species of fish, species $1$, species $2$, and species $3$, are believed to co-exist in equal proportion in a particular river. A random sample of fish is conducted, and the frequency distribution of the fish in the sample is shown below.\n\n| Species of Fish $(y_{i})$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Observed Frequency $(O_{i})$ | $89$ | $120$ | $91$ |\n\nA chi-square goodness of fit test is conducted at the $5%$ significance level with the following null and alternative hypotheses:\n\n- $H_{0}$: The fish species are distributed uniformly.\n- $H_{1}$: The fish species are not distributed uniformly.\n\nThe table below gives the values of $w$ that satisfy $P(W \\ge w) = p$, where $W\u223c\u03c7^{2}(\u03bd)$.\n\n| $\u03bd\u2216p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $1$ | $2.705$ | $3.841$ | $5.024$ | $6.635$ | $7.879$ |\n| $2$ | $4.605$ | $5.991$ | $7.378$ | $9.210$ | $10.597$ |\n| $3$ | $6.251$ | $7.815$ | $9.348$ | $11.345$ | $12.838$ |\n\nUsing this information, select the options that make the following statements true.\n\nThe test statistic is\n{{field-1}}.\n\nThe number of degrees of freedom for this test is $\u03bd =$ {{field-2}}.\n\nAt the $5%$ significance level, there is {{field-3}} evidence to reject the null hypothesis.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
