      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-252497",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose $Y$ is a random variable with support $S = {2, 3, 5, 7, 9}$. A random sample is carried out, and the sample data is shown below.\n\n| Observation $(y_{i})$ | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ | $7$ | $9$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Observed Frequency $(O_{i})$ | $36$ | $48$ | $49$ | $40$ | $27$ |\n\nA chi-square goodness of fit test is conducted at the $10%$ significance level with the following null and alternative hypotheses:\n\n- $H_{0}:Y\u223cU{2, 3, 5, 7, 9}$\n- $H_{1}:Y\u2241U{2, 3, 5, 7, 9}$\n\nThe table below gives the values of $w$ that satisfy $P(W \\ge w) = p$, where $W\u223c\u03c7^{2}(\u03bd)$.\n\n| $\u03bd\u2216p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $3$ | $6.251$ | $7.815$ | $9.348$ | $11.345$ | $12.838$ |\n| $4$ | $7.779$ | $9.488$ | $11.143$ | $13.277$ | $14.860$ |\n| $5$ | $9.236$ | $11.070$ | $12.833$ | $15.086$ | $16.750$ |\n\nUsing this information, select the options that make the following statements true.\n\nThe test statistic is\n{{field-1}}.\n\nThe number of degrees of freedom for this test is $\u03bd =$ {{field-2}}.\n\nAt the $10%$ significance level, there is {{field-3}} evidence to reject the null hypothesis.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
